pect Avatar merit?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of a Mage that just gets really detailed, fully-formed, ideas out of complete nowhere that just so happens to be the EXACT thing they need to solve the current problem. Your classic gumshoe's revelation.</div> </div> </div> </div>A high level of coincidence in the Mage\u2019s life would work well, though it should be one part help and one part inconvenience. A high level avatar, in my opinion, should have desires and motivations even if they are circumspect about it.<br /> <br /> Some of the perception effects of Shadows in Wraith would work well here, since you can build a very strong and yet very subtle Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}